course: dictionary
lesson: 6240
title: One short word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «mod» is short, but it has several meanings. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which one is right. In a game, «a Minecraft mod» is an add-on that players make, so the topic is a game.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about a chat room or a game server, mod probably means moderator, the helper who keeps things polite. If it is about numbers, as in «12 mod 3 = 0», mod means the remainder after dividing.
explain: Mod is short for other words, such as modification, moderator and modern. «Mod cons» (UK) means modern conveniences, like a dishwasher or heating. Once you know the topic, you can pick the meaning that fits.
fact: A mod is a change or add-on made to a game or machine by players, not by the makers.
fact: «Mod» can also mean a moderator, a person who keeps an online chat, forum or game server safe and polite.
fact: In maths and coding, «mod» gives the remainder after division: 17 mod 5 = 2.
fact: Always ask a parent before downloading a game mod, and use official stores, because some unknown downloads can carry viruses.
fact: Mods were young people in Britain in the time of the Beatles, known for smart suits and scooters.
exercise: In «a Minecraft mod», what is a mod? | *A change or add-on made to a game by players | A helper who keeps the chat polite | A modern kitchen appliance like a dishwasher
exercise: What is 13 mod 4? | *1 | 4 | 3 | 0
exercise: A player asks Priya for her password. What should she do? | *Say no and tell a parent | Give it, because mods are always right | Download a mod to check the player | Tell the player her password is easy to guess
test: «Mod cons» in a house means what? | A type of dance | *Modern conveniences, like a dishwasher or heating | A kind of scooter | Old furniture
test: What does «n mod 2 = 0» tell you about the number n? | It is the biggest number | *It leaves remainder 0 when divided by 2, so n is even | It is a moderator in a chat | It is a game mod
exam: Which best describes the Mods in Britain at the time of the Beatles? | Adults who ran online games | *Young people in smart suits who rode scooters | Teachers who checked homework | People who made computer games
